gsndesign:dd-0283
    a gsndesign:RetiredDecision ;
    gsndesign:retirementReason "Superseded in 1.2.4. The domain named only gsn:ArtefactReference, which made gsn:InstantiationDataReference unable to say what data it points at even though the standard describes it as \"a reference to the information used to instantiate the template argument\". Typing an IDR as an ArtefactReference to work around this is not available: ArtefactReference is a subclass of GSNElement, so it would oblige every IDR to carry a schema:identifier and to be an element of the notation, which an instantiation data reference is not. Widening the domain to the union is the narrower change."@en ;
    gsndesign:supersededBy gsndesign:dd-0960 ;
    gsndesign:positionKey "S04.R121b" ;
    gsndesign:part gsndesign:part-1 ;
    gsndesign:section gsndesign:sec-core ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:OWL ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "Only an artefact reference can refer to something."@en ;
    gsndesign:nlWrittenFor "44d96ac6" ;
    prov:used gsndesign:src-0085 ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsndesign:why-0049 ;
    prov:generated gsndesign:st-0283 .

