#    Drafts. Each still needs a source passage and a rationale written by hand.
#################################################################

gsndesign:why-0213
    a gsndesign:Rationale ;
    gsndesign:rationaleText """The top goal is the pinnacle claim of an argument, not of the whole store. The general class axiom said otherwise: it made a goal top exactly when no goal or strategy anywhere supports it, so an away goal - the top goal of its own module, referenced from another - was disqualified by the very reference that makes it an away goal. Scoping the parent test to the module is a condition relating three individuals (parent, goal, module) and is not expressible as an OWL class expression, so the axiom was weakened to hold in one direction only and the scoped definition moved here and into rule S06, where it can be stated.

A parent is discounted exactly when some module contains the parent and not the goal. Written as containment rather than gsn:inModule so that the constraint does not depend on rules S53 and S54 having run. With no modules in the graph nothing is discounted, so a core-only case behaves exactly as it did before.

A goal that challenges something is excluded as well. Nothing supports a defeater, precisely because it is levied against the argument rather than part of it, and the unscoped reading therefore made every challenge goal a top goal - which is not the claim the author is asserting."""@en .

gsndesign:dd-0968
    a gsndesign:DesignDecision ;
    gsndesign:positionKey "S04.SH072" ;
    gsndesign:part gsndesign:part-1 ;
    gsndesign:section gsndesign:sec-core ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:SHACL ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "A goal marked as a top goal must not be supported by a goal or strategy of its own module, and must not challenge any part of the argument."@en ;
    gsndesign:nlWrittenFor "3b2a58ff" ;
    gsndesign:hasRationale gsndesign:why-0213 ;
    prov:generated gsndesign:st-0968 .

gsndesign:st-0968
    a gsndesign:StatementRecord ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy gsndesign:dd-0968 ;
    gsndesign:inGraph gsndesign:shapes-1.0.3 ;
    gsndesign:statementText """gsnsh:TopGoalHasNoParentShape gsn:coreOrExtension "Core GSN"@en ;
    rdf:type sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment "From the general class axiom: ( Goal and not (inverse gsn:supportedBy some (Goal or Strategy)) and not (gsn:challenges some Thing) ) SubClassOf ( gsn:top value true ). A strategy counts as a parent: a goal reached through a strategy is not the pinnacle claim, and reading the axiom over goals alone made every strategy-parented goal a top goal. A parent in another module does not count: the top goal is the pinnacle claim of an argument, not of the whole store, so an away goal supported from elsewhere remains the top goal of its own module. That scoping is a condition on three individuals and cannot be written as an OWL class expression, which is why the axiom holds in one direction only and this shape carries the other."@en ;
    rdfs:label "Top goal has no supported parent goal in scope"@en ;
    sh:severity sh:Violation ;
    sh:targetClass gsn:Goal .""" ;
    gsndesign:statementChecksum "3b2a58ff" ;
    gsndesign:structuralKey "gsnsh:TopGoalHasNoParentShape|node|" ;
    gsndesign:aboutTerm gsnsh:TopGoalHasNoParentShape ;
    gsndesign:mentionsTerm gsn:Goal ,
        gsn:challenges ,
        gsn:coreOrExtension ,
        gsn:supportedBy ,
        gsn:top ,
        gsnsh:TopGoalHasNoParentShape .

