#################################################################
#    Added by hand (1 rationale)
#    Written for two decisions that carried gsndesign:noRationaleRecorded.
#################################################################

gsndesign:why-0214
    a gsndesign:Rationale ;
    gsndesign:rationaleText """The ontology's range for gsn:minCardinality and gsn:maxCardinality is xsd:nonNegativeInteger and
stays that way, but the shape cannot require that exact datatype IRI. A hand-written 1 is
xsd:integer by Turtle's rules, and pyoxigraph - the engine ontology/queries/ and ontology/queries/rules/ are executed
against - normalises every derived integer type to xsd:integer on load, so even a correctly typed
literal arrives at the validator as one. Non-negativity is what the axiom is actually about, so the
shape admits either datatype and checks the value directly with sh:minInclusive."""@en .


